acceptance_criteria: The database wrapper bootstraps the schema before spawning coverage; workers skip redundant DDL only after an explicit ready handoff; missing PostgreSQL still fails closed; the full release gate passes against a fresh throwaway database
parent: pm-web-9ulj
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "npm run release:check with the repository throwaway PostgreSQL database on 2026-08-06"
repro_steps: "Run npm run db:up, then npm run release:check. Parallel route workers each call initSchema while peers execute DML, producing PostgreSQL 40P01 deadlocks."
resolution: "The test wrapper now initializes the production schema in a dedicated process before node:test starts parallel workers, then hands workers an explicit ready marker; direct test invocations still initialize once locally."
expected_result: Parallel real-Postgres route coverage starts only after DDL completes and remains fail-closed when PostgreSQL is unavailable.
actual_result: "A fresh throwaway PostgreSQL run completed 260/260 tests with no 40P01 deadlocks; release:check, production audit, package dry-run, and changelog verification all passed."
